{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_1391207909#3_2762294019","relevance":2,"reason":"The passage directly mentions bee sting therapy and reports no improvement in quality of life, but the document is about bee sting therapy for multiple sclerosis rather than the quality-of-life impact of bee stings themselves.","learned":"Bee sting therapy in a small MS study showed no MRI benefit and participants reported no improvement in disability, fatigue, or quality of life."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ bee honeybee hymenoptera) (+ sting stings) \"quality of life\" (+ allergy allergic anaphylaxis venom))","reason":"Search for focused evidence on Hymenoptera/bee sting allergy and quality-of-life outcomes, which is more likely to directly answer the information need."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ bee honeybee hymenoptera) (+ sting stings) \"quality of life\" (+ allergy allergic anaphylaxis venom))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_05_1004088852#13_1823916429","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q1046","rank":1,"snippet":"stings? What is the treatment for bee and wasp stings? Prevention Treatment of localised site reactions Treatment for systemic reactions Venom immunotherapy desensitisation What is the outcome for bee and wasp stings? Related information Bibliography On DermNet NZ Other websites Skin cancer Dermatology Made Easy Book Call for sponsors Sign up to the newsletter \" , \"segment\": \"Protection usually lasts 1–3 years after discontinuation. Insect venoms are commercially available for honey <cover>bee, paper wasp, and yellow jacket European wasp. A Cochrane review reported venom immunotherapy significantly reduces the risk of systemic and large local reactions, and is likely to reduce the risk of anaphylaxis, improving quality of life. Venom immunotherapy can be recommended for: Children with systemic sting </cover>reactions not limited to the skin Adults with systemic reactions including those limited to the skin High risk factors including beekeepers, patients with clonal mast cell disorders Impaired quality of life following sting reactions NOT recommended for toxic reactions or those sensitised but with no clinical symptoms. What is the outcome for bee and wasp stings? The majority of bee and wasp sting reactions are localised and resolve in hours to days. Episodes are usually rare and "}}
