{"latest_judgment":{"docno":null,"relevance":0,"reason":"No new unskipped result to judge; the exact 'bee sting reactions' and quality-of-life query returned only previously judged Verywell bee-sting reaction segments.","learned":"The precise phrase query did not add new evidence beyond the already found source stating swelling from frequent bee stings can disrupt quality of life or work."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"bee sting allergy\" \"quality of life\")","reason":"Search the common phrase 'bee sting allergy' paired with quality of life to find additional dedicated patient or clinical pages beyond the previously retrieved reaction overview."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"bee sting allergy\" \"quality of life\")"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_10_693948946#2_1288968336","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q1056","rank":1,"snippet":"Safe for Weight Loss? Vitamin K: How Much Do You Need? Fiber for Heart, Cholesterol, and Digestive Health Are You Getting the Vitamins You Need? WebMD Special Sections \" , \"segment\": \"Likely Effective for<cover>Bee sting allergy. A series of bee venom shots under the skin (bee venom immunotherapy) seems to be effective for reducing reactions to bee stings in people with severe allergy to bee stings. Bee venom immunotherapy provides 98% to 99% protection from reactions to bee stings. Once immunotherapy is stopped, the risk of reaction over the next 5 to 10 years is about 5% to 15%. Purified bee venom for under-the- skin injection is an FDA approved product. Possibly Ineffective for Multiple sclerosis (MS). Administering live bee stings in gradually increasing doses up to 20 stings given three times weekly does not seem to improve multiples sclerosis. Treatment for 24 weeks does not seem to improve fatigue, disability, or quality of life. </cover>Insufficient Evidence for Stiffness and pain in the shoulder joint (frozen shoulder). Early research suggests that receiving dilute bee venom injections might improve pain and disability in people with frozen shoulder.\" , \"start_char\": "}}
