{"latest_judgment":{"docno":null,"relevance":0,"reason":"No new unskipped result to judge; the 'impaired quality of life' query returned only previously judged DermNet bee/wasp sting segments.","learned":"The exact 'impaired quality of life' wording mainly recovers the DermNet evidence already found."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ hymenoptera bee wasp) (+ sting stings venom) (+ anxiety fear) (+ social restriction))","reason":"Search directly for the anxiety/fear and social-restriction mechanism by which bee/Hymenoptera sting reactions affect quality of life, without requiring the exact quality-of-life phrase."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ hymenoptera bee wasp) (+ sting stings venom) (+ anxiety fear) (+ social restriction))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_11_704929422#3_1304533676","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1058","rank":3,"snippet":"Sting? Social Wasps Paper Wasps Yellowjackets Hornets Solitary Wasps Cicada Killers Cricket Hunter Wasps Mud Daubers Tips for Professionals \" , \"segment\": \"Vespid wasp nests are constructed of a paper-like material and may be found either above or below ground. Another important group of wasps with stingers are the solitary wasps. The stinger of solitary wasps is used primarily for subduing prey. Although solitary wasps may be common and are often thought dangerous by people who <cover>fear wasps, solitary wasps rarely sting humans. Most are entirely beneficial, feeding on spiders, crickets, cicadas and caterpillars. Knowing how to distinguish between solitary and social wasps can be useful in determining whether control is justified. Wasp </cover>Stings Wasps sting their victims and inject venom from the rear of the abdomen (tail). The stinger in all wasps and bees is a modified egg-laying organ (ovipositor); hence only females can sting. Venom from ant, bee and wasp stings is responsible for 40 to 100 deaths per year in the United States.\" , \"start_char\": 1845.000000 , \"title\": \"Paper Wasps, Yellowjackets and Solitary Wasps - Do solitary wasps sting?\"","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_05_1004088852#7_1823900839","rank":1,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_05_1004088852#8_1823903949","rank":2,"relevance":3}]}}
