{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ bee wasp hymenoptera) (+ sting stings venom) anaphylaxis \"quality of life\")"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_1391207909#4_2762295856","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1069","rank":8,"snippet":"\"The participants also noted no improvement in their disability, fatigue, or <cover>quality of life. 3 ﻿ Despite a lack of scientific evidence, bee sting therapy has been reported anecdotally by some people with MS to increase stability, as well as reduce fatigue and spasticity, which are common symptoms of MS . Risks of Bee Sting Therapy Pain is one of the biggest drawbacks with bee sting therapy. In addition to the discomfort of being stung by 40 bees, most people experience some degree of swelling and redness at the sting site. This swelling and pain can generally be eased by applying ice before and after the stings. Other adverse effects reported include: 4 ﻿ Itching Hives Fatigue Anxiety Cough Headache Loss of appetite Yellowing of the white part of the eyes (called jaundice) Severe pain in the left shoulder and arm and chest wall Muscle weakness of the left arm and hand. Rarely, these very serious and severe effects below have also been reported: Death A small number of people (less than 100) die every year from reactions to bee stings. 5 ﻿ These deaths could be due to anaphylaxis (</cover>severe allergic reactions) or heart attacks brought on by a mild allergic reaction ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_05_1004088852#13_1823916429","rank":1,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_05_1004088852#12_1823913740","rank":2,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_1391180600#12_2762248206","rank":3,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_03_1067819329#4_1802449718","rank":4,"relevance":2},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_1391180600#11_2762246097","rank":5,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_05_1004088852#7_1823900839","rank":6,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_00_193756478#1_336780475","rank":7,"relevance":2}]}}
