{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ venom allergy \"quality of life\" (+ bee wasp hymenoptera sting stings))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_51_1681810333#3_3172669123","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1077","rank":7,"snippet":"of Allergy and Clinical Immunology: In Practice Review and Feature Article Fatal Anaphylaxis: Mortality Rate and Risk Factors Key words Abbreviation used Information for Category 1 CME Credit Learning objectives: Fatal Drug Anaphylaxis Epidemiology Risk factors Practical implications of fatal drug anaphylaxis data Fatal Food Anaphylaxis Epidemiology Risk factors—food Practical implications of fatal food anaphylaxis data Fatal Venom Anaphylaxis Epidemiology Risk factors—venom Practical implications of fatal <cover>venom anaphylaxis data Conclusions References \" , \"segment\": \"The rarity of fatal anaphylaxis and the significant quality of life impact of allergic conditions suggest that quality of life impairment should be a key consideration when making treatment decisions in patients at risk for anaphylaxis. Previous article in issue Next article in issue Key words Anaphylaxis Mortality Insect sting Food allergy</cover>Drug allergy Abbreviation used ICD International Classification of Diseases Information for Category 1 CME Credit Credit can now be obtained, free for a limited time, by reading the review articles in this issue. Please note the following instructions. Method of Physician Participation in Learning Process: The core material for these activities can be read in this issue of the Journal or online at the JACI: In Practice Web ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_778278917#16_1605639199","rank":1,"relevance":2},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_03_1067819329#4_1802449718","rank":2,"relevance":2},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_1391180600#12_2762248206","rank":3,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_32_853332099#12_1643577752","rank":4,"relevance":1},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_05_1004088852#8_1823903949","rank":5,"relevance