{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ beekeeper beekeepers) (+ bee honeybee) (+ sting stings venom allergy) \"quality of life\")"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_51_957197831#4_2002933298","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1092","rank":3,"snippet":"Precautions & Warnings: Are there any interactions with medications? Dosing considerations for Bee Venom. QUESTION Report Problems to the Food and Drug Administration Health Solutions From Our Sponsors \" , \"segment\": \"Purified bee venom for under-the-skin injection is an FDA approved product. SLIDESHOW Could I Be Allergic? Discover Your Allergy Triggers See Slideshow Possibly Ineffective for... Arthritis. People used to think that bee venom might be a useful treatment for arthritis. This theory was largely due to supposed swelling-reducing ( anti- inflammatory) effects of bee venom and the observation that many <cover>beekeepers don't develop arthritis. However, research results have not supported this. Multiple sclerosis (MS). Administering live bee stings in gradually increasing doses up to 20 stings given three times weekly does not seem to improve multiples sclerosis. Treatment for 24 weeks does not seem to improve fatigue, disability, or quality of life. </cover>Insufficient Evidence to Rate Effectiveness for... Nerve pain.\" , \"start_char\": 1778.000000 , \"title\": \"Bee Venom: Health Benefits, Uses, Side Effects, Dosage & Interactions\" , \"url\": \"https://www.rxlist.com/bee_venom/supplements.htm\" }","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_05_1004088852#13_1823916429","rank":1,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_05_1004088852#12_1823913740","rank":2,"relevance":3}]}}
