{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_06_1404027808#0_1929472654","relevance":2,"reason":"The result is dedicated to bee sting allergy and directly describes symptoms including pain/itching and potentially severe anaphylaxis requiring immediate medical attention, but the snippet does not explicitly discuss quality of life, anxiety, work/social restriction, or daily functioning.","learned":"Bee stings are usually not serious, but in allergic people or after multiple stings they can cause severe anaphylaxis requiring immediate medical attention, along with local pain and itching."},"action":{"op":"document","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_06_1404027808#0_1929472654","reason":"The snippet is a dedicated bee-sting allergy page and may contain fuller evidence on symptoms, prevention, emergency care, or lifestyle effects that would more directly support how bee stings affect quality of life."}}
{"request":{"op":"document","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_06_1404027808#0_1929472654"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_06_1404027808#0_1929472654","document":"Bee Sting Allergy: Symptoms of Anaphylaxis ... Bee Sting Allergy: Symptoms of Anaphylaxis Bee Sting Allergy: Symptoms of Anaphylaxis What causes a bee sting allergy? What are the symptoms of bee sting allergy? Who is at risk for bee sting allergy? When to seek help First aid: Treating bee stings at home Medical treatment Bee sting prevention  ... Bee Sting Allergy: Symptoms of Anaphylaxis Bee Sting Allergy: Symptoms of Anaphylaxis Medically reviewed by Marc Meth, MD, FACAAI, FAAAI — Written by Robin Madell — Updated on April 20, 2021 Symptoms Risk factors When to seek help First aid Medical treatment Prevention What causes a bee sting allergy? Usually, bee stings don’t cause a serious reaction. However, if you’re allergic to bee stings or have had several bee stings, you may experience a severe reaction such as anaphylaxis. Anaphylaxis to a bee sting requires immediate medical attention. What are the symptoms of bee sting allergy? Mild, local symptoms of a bee sting include: pain or itching at the site of the sting a white spot where the stinger punctured the skin redness and slight swelling around the sting Severe (allergic) systemic symptoms of a bee sting include: hives flushed or pale skin swelling of the throat, face, and lips headache dizziness or fainting nausea and vomiting abdominal cramping and diarrhea difficulty breathing or swallowing decrease in blood pressure weak and rapid heart rate loss of consciousness Who is at risk for bee sting allergy?","ok":true,"op":"document"}}
