{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_10_616793458#5_1141009235","relevance":2,"reason":"The WebMD document is dedicated to insect stings and bee-sting allergy and directly lists painful local reactions, swelling, itching, severe allergic/anaphylactic symptoms, restlessness/anxiety, emergency treatment, and life-threatening risk. However, it does not explicitly discuss quality of life, daily function, work, or social restriction.","learned":"Bee-sting allergy can affect people through pain, swelling, itching, anxiety/restlessness, breathing or swallowing difficulty, dizziness, gastrointestinal symptoms, and potentially life-threatening reactions needing emergency care."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"bee sting allergy\" (+ \"daily life\" lifestyle \"quality of life\" anxiety fear work))","reason":"Search for dedicated bee-sting allergy sources that explicitly connect reactions or fear of stings to daily life, lifestyle, work, anxiety, or quality-of-life impairment."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"bee sting allergy\" (+ \"daily life\" lifestyle \"quality of life\" anxiety fear work))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_1391197464#9_2762268863","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q1113","rank":1,"snippet":"sting? A Word From Verywell \" , \"segment\": \"Take over-the-counter anti-inflammatory drugs ( Advil, Aleve ). Under Your Skin In the unlikely case that part or all of a stinger has become lodged underneath the skin, it will probably work its way out over a few days much like a splinter. If the swelling doesn't go down after a couple of days, you may need to see a doctor to check for infection. How to Treat <cover>Bee Sting Allergy Home Remedies A lot of home remedies may help ease the pain, itching, and swelling of a bee sting. Many of these aren't backed by science but some people claim they work. </cover>Apple cider vinegar: Some people claim that it neutralizes venom and helps reduce swelling. You can soak the sting in diluted vinegar or cover it with a vinegar-soaked cloth for 15 minutes. Honey: It may seem ironic, but this bee product is shown to improve wound healing, reduce inflammation, and kill germs that could cause an infection.\" , \"start_char\": 5180.000000 , \"title\": \"How to Remove a Bee Stinger and "}}
