{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_10_616697030#5_1140802969","relevance":2,"reason":"The WebMD page is dedicated to insect stings and bee-sting allergy and directly lists symptoms such as pain, swelling, itching, hives, trouble breathing/swallowing, restlessness/anxiety, dizziness, low blood pressure, emergency treatment, and life-threatening risk. However, it does not explicitly discuss quality of life, daily function, work, or social restriction.","learned":"Bee/insect sting allergy can cause painful local symptoms, anxiety/restlessness, systemic anaphylactic symptoms, emergency-treatment needs, and life-threatening reactions."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"bee stings\" \"quality of life\" (+ anxiety swelling anaphylaxis work))","reason":"Search a focused plural bee-stings query with quality-of-life mechanisms to find additional direct sources beyond the already exhausted exact singular and treatment-focused queries."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"bee stings\" \"quality of life\" (+ anxiety swelling anaphylaxis work))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_51_957197831#5_2002934849","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q1121","rank":1,"snippet":"known by? What is Bee Venom? Likely Effective for... SLIDESHOW Possibly Ineffective for... Insufficient Evidence to Rate Effectiveness for... How does Bee Venom work? Are there safety concerns? Special Precautions & Warnings: Are there any interactions with medications? Dosing considerations for Bee Venom. QUESTION Report Problems to the Food and Drug Administration Health Solutions From Our Sponsors \" , \"segment\": \"However, research results have not supported this. Multiple sclerosis (MS). Administering live <cover>bee stings in gradually increasing doses up to 20 stings given three times weekly does not seem to improve multiples sclerosis. Treatment for 24 weeks does not seem to improve fatigue, disability, or quality of life. Insufficient Evidence to Rate Effectiveness for... Nerve pain. Painful, swollen tendons (tendonitis). Muscle swelling (</cover>inflammation). More evidence is needed to rate the effectiveness of bee venom for these uses. How does Bee Venom work? Giving repeated and controlled injections of bee venom under the skin causes the immune system to get used to bee venom, and helps reduce the severity of an allergy to bee venom.\" , \"start_char\": 2215.000000 , \"title\": \"Bee Venom: Health Benefits, Uses, Side "}}
