{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_07_571733127#11_990044617","relevance":1,"reason":"The passage mentions insect venom allergy, throat tightness, shortness of breath, anxiety, and emergency treatment after stings, but the document is about causes of throat tightness rather than bee stings or quality-of-life impact.","learned":"Insect venom allergy can cause throat swelling/tightness, shortness of breath, anxiety, and confusion, but this source is not focused on quality of life."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1122","reason":"This query targets venom allergy with anxiety/fear and immunotherapy; despite the first off-topic result, later results may include dedicated sting-allergy sources discussing psychological burden or treatment benefits."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1122"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_06_640067049#9_1147801929","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1122","rank":2,"snippet":", \"segment\": \". Another option is to make a soil pile in a similarly sunny area and allow bees to nest in it. Bare patches for ground-nesting bees are becoming more difficult for them to find, so anything you can do is going to be beneficial! How to Control These Ground Nesting Bees: Before you decide to evict your bees, consider this. These bees serve an important purpose as pollinators. They're not aggressive, and in most cases, you can still mow your lawn and continue your regular outdoor activities without <cover>fear of being stung. And nesting activity is limited to spring, so bees won't stay for long. Unless you have concerns for a family member with a bee venom allergy, </cover>it's usually preferable to leave Ground or Digger Bees alone. Ground and Digger Bees nest in dry soil, and avoid damp areas when choosing nest sites.\" , \"start_char\": 3302.000000 , \"title\": \"Ground Bees are beneficial insects that perform an important role as pollinators\" , \"url\": \"http://www.gardening-for-wildlife.com/ground-bees.html\" }"}}
